======================================================================================
BLOCK 2 -- the covering lemma, exact
======================================================================================
    Lemma (covering).  Let 0 < r < 1 and let the digit set be {0,1,...,n} with
    L := n/(1-r).  If 1 <= r L  then  E := { sum_{i>=0} u_i r^i : u_i in {0..n} } = [0, L].
    Proof: E = {0..n} + r E and E is compact with min 0, max L; the n+1 intervals
    [u + 0, u + rL] have consecutive left endpoints one apart and length rL >= 1, so their
    union is [0, n + rL] = [0, L] (n + rL = n + rn/(1-r) = n/(1-r) = L).  So [0,L] is a
    fixed point of the Hutchinson operator of the IFS {x -> r x + u}, which is a
    contraction on the compact sets: E = [0,L].
    [ok ] L = 2/(1-rho) = 2 + sqrt2  L = 3.414213562373
    [ok ] covering condition  1 <= rho L  (digit step 1, digits {0,1,2})  rho L = 1.414213562373 = sqrt2
    [ok ] rho L = sqrt2 exactly
    [ok ] slack in the covering condition: rho >= 1/3  rho - 1/3 = 0.080880
    [ok ] the lemma's two identities: n + rho L = L with n = 2  so [0,L] is the attractor and E = [0, 2+sqrt2]
    [ok ] {0,1} + rho[0,L] = [0, 1 + rho L] = [0, 1+sqrt2]  (needs rho L >= 1)
    [ok ] (S2) at depth 10: B_n = A0_n - sum_{m odd} rho^m, as sets  1024 points, exact in Z[sqrt2]
    [ok ] (S3) at depth 10: A0_n + rho A0_n = {0,1} + rho E_n, digits {0,1,2}  13859 distinct values on each side, exact
    [ok ] C - K = sqrt2 [0, 1+sqrt2] - sqrt2/2 = [-sqrt2/2, 2+sqrt2/2]  [-0.707106781187, 2.707106781187]
    [ok ] length(C - K) = 2 + sqrt2  = 3.414213562373
    [ok ] length(C - K) = 1 + diam K  (so the hull is filled, not merely covered)
    [ok ] GATE G-1: length >= 1, hence X(1+sqrt2) = (C-K) mod 1 = T  margin 2.414213562373 over the threshold 1

======================================================================================
BLOCK 3 -- constructive check against the ORIGINAL definitions
======================================================================================
    The proof is constructive: it produces, for each y in [-sqrt2/2, 2+sqrt2/2], a pair
    of one-sided words (eps, delta) with y = pi(eps) - w(delta) exactly.  This block runs
    that construction on a grid of targets and evaluates pi and w from their definitions
    in M1 (Lemma 1 and Lemma 3), independently of every identity above.
    [ok ] greedy witness reproduces y on a 4001-point grid of [-sqrt2/2, 2+sqrt2/2]  max |pi(eps) - w(delta) - y| = 1.332e-15
    [ok ] witness words are 0/1 sequences (shown at y = 0.3)  eps[1:9] = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], delta[0:8] = [0, 1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1]
    [ok ] the hull is exactly [min C - max K, max C - min K] = [-P, 1+Q]  [-0.707107, 2.707107]

======================================================================================
BLOCK 4 -- the T-T route (Theorem T) re-derived exactly, and one correction
======================================================================================
    [ok ] tau(C) = 1/(alpha-2) = 1+sqrt2  tau(C) = 2.414213562373
    [ok ] tau(K) = rho/(1-2rho) = 1+sqrt2  tau(K) = 2.414213562373
    [ok ] tau(C) tau(K) = 3+2sqrt2 >= 1  product = 5.828427124746
    [ok ] gap_max(C) = (alpha-2)/alpha = 3-2sqrt2  = 0.171572875254
    [ok ] gap_max(K) = sqrt2-1  = 0.414213562373
    [ok ] side condition A: diam K > gap_max(C)  2.414214 > 0.171573
    [ok ] side condition B: diam C = 1 > gap_max(K)  1 > 0.414214
    [ok ] the two routes agree on the LENGTH of C-K
    CORRECTION (R0, 2026-08-26).  plans/plan-1061.html states Theorem T's conclusion as
    "C-K is the interval [-diam K, 1], of length >= 2".  The length is right; the endpoints
    are not, and the same slip is in the T-T paragraph of the M4 row.  K straddles 0
    (P = sqrt2/2 > 0 and Q = 1+sqrt2/2 > 0 are BOTH positive at every alpha with
    alphabar < 0), so the hull of C-K is [min C - max K, max C - min K] = [-P, 1+Q], which
    is [-0.707107, 2.707107] here, not [-2.414214, 1].  Nothing downstream depends on the
    endpoints -- the conclusion X = T only needs the length -- but the statement should be
    corrected where it appears.

